        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Manhattan Community Board 6\n- Places: Gramercy Park, Stuyvesant Town, Peter Cooper Village, Waterside Plaza, Murray Hill, Kips Bay, Turtle Bay, Tudor City, Sutton Place, Manhattan, East River\n- Projects: Tudor City\n- Events: Construction, boundary definition\n\nFacts:\n- In 1927, construction of Tudor City commenced, making Tudor City the first residential skyscraper complex in the world.\n- In 1999, Manhattan Community Board 6 defined Murray Hill's boundaries as East 34th Street on the south, East 40th Street on the north, Madison Avenue on the west, and the East River on the east.\n- Manhattan Community Board 6 includes the neighborhoods of Gramercy Park, Stuyvesant Town, Peter Cooper Village, Waterside Plaza, Murray Hill, Kips Bay, Turtle Bay, Tudor City, and Sutton Place.",
